<article id="post-15246" class="post-15246 post type-post status-publish format-standard has-post-thumbnail hentry category-skincare" itemtype="https://schema.org/CreativeWork" itemscope>
	<div class="inside-article">
				<div class="featured-image page-header-image-single grid-container grid-parent">
			<img width="400" height="267" src="https://jarxi.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/05/featured-1322.jpg" class="attachment-full size-full wp-post-image" alt="person holding white plastic container" itemprop="image" decoding="async" fetchpriority="high" srcset="https://jarxi.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/05/featured-1322.jpg 400w, https://jarxi.com/wp-content/uploads/2026/05/featured-1322-300x200.jpg 300w" sizes="(max-width: 400px) 100vw, 400px" />		</div>
					<header class="entry-header">
				<h1 class="entry-title" itemprop="headline">Is Experiment Beauty Super Saturated Serum Worth the Hype?</h1>		<div class="entry-meta">
			<span class="posted-on"><time class="updated" datetime="" itemprop="dateModified"></time><time class="entry-date published" datetime="" itemprop="datePublished"></time></span> <span class="byline">作者 <span class="author vcard" itemprop="author" itemtype="https://schema.org/Person" itemscope><a class="url fn n" href="https://jarxi.com/author/jarxi/" title="查看发表的所有文章" rel="author" itemprop="url"><span class="author-name" itemprop="name"></span></a></span></span> 		</div>
					</header>
			
		<div class="entry-content" itemprop="text">
			<div class="brp-wrap">
<div class="brp-hero">
<div class="brp-tag">30-Day Test</div>
<div class="brp-hook">I replaced my entire morning routine with this single serum — here&#8217;s what happened to my skin after 30 days.</div>
<div class="brp-sub">Expert Analysis · Honest Reviews · Real Results</div>
</div>
<div class="brp-content">🧴 **Ditched My Whole Routine**<br />
I stopped using moisturizer, toner, and eye cream for 30 days. Just this serum, splashed on wet skin, morning only. My dehydrated forehead lines? Still there — but way less angry.</p>
<p>The real test: I flew to Denver (humidity: 0%) and my skin didn’t peel. That’s never happened.</p>
<p>&#8212;</p>
<p>📸 **What You’re Actually Buying**<br />
It’s a 30ml bottle of pure hydration tech. $38. The claim that hooked me: “one-step morning routine.” I’m lazy, so I bit.</p>
<p>1. **Super Saturated Base** — 5% glycerin + polyglutamic acid. Sounds boring. Works like a drink of water.<br />
2. **Adaptogenic Mushrooms** — Tremella + snow mushroom. They hold more water than hyaluronic acid without the sticky feel.<br />
3. **No Frills Formula** — No fragrance, no oils, no silicones. Just wetness.</p>
<p>&#8212;</p>
<p>🔬 **The Nerd Stuff**<br />
Hero ingredients: Polyglutamic acid (holds 4x more water than HA) and tremella mushroom (fits through skin pores better than HA ever will). Plus 5% glycerin — old reliable. No random plant extracts for marketing.</p>
<p>• Polyglutamic Acid: Hydrates deeper, lasts longer<br />
• Tremella Mushroom: Sinks in fast, zero tackiness<br />
• Glycerin: The backbone of every good moisturizer<br />
• Snow Mushroom: Seals it all in without weight</p>
<p>&#8212;</p>
<p>📉 **30 Days of Wet Face**<br />
Texture: straight-up water. Drops off your finger if you’re not fast. Absorbs in 10 seconds on damp skin. Smells like nothing — which I love.</p>
<p>Week 2: I got a pimple. Waited it out. Week 3: my skin looked… bouncy? Not dewy-greasy, just healthy. One shock: it pills under sunscreen if you let it dry too long.</p>
<p>💡 **One Thing** Apply to soaking wet skin — like, dripping face. Pat don’t rub. Wait 20 seconds then sunscreen. No moisturizer needed.</p>
<p>&#8212;</p>
<p>💡 **Who This Is For**<br />
My skin looks calmer. Redness is down 40%. But my dark circles? Unchanged. And it won’t fix dry patches from retinol — you still need a cream at night.</p>
<p>✅ **Buy if** You’re combo/oily and hate heavy moisturizers<br />
⏭️ **Skip if** You’re dry as dust and need thick creams<br />
💰 **Worth it?** Yes — $38 for 30 days of one-step mornings. That’s cheap therapy.</p>
<p>&#8212;</p>
<p>🏆 **Final Call**<br />
If you want to streamline your morning to 30 seconds and still look hydrated, buy it. If you like layering seven products for fun, skip it.</p>
<p>**7.8/10** — Best hydrating shortcut I’ve tried</p>
<p>🛍️ **Where to Buy** Experiment Beauty’s site directly. Grab the mini first ($18) if you’re skeptical — it lasts 3 weeks.</p></div>
